Home Lab #1: Setting Up a Windows 11 VM with Virtual Box (and Fixing What Went Wrong)”
Setup Windows 11 using VM Ware

VirtualBox 7, Windows 11 Pro, 8 GB RAM, 3 CPUs, 64 GB dynamic disk, EFI + TPM 2.0 + Secure Boot
Issue 1: “failed to boot”, ISO not attached (download incomplete) → rebuilt VM
Issue 2: missed the boot prompt → UEFI menu → Boot Manager → CD-ROM
Manual install: no product key, Pro edition, custom install
Didn't have any issues when setting up Kali VM.

I created the VM before the download had finished, so there was no ISO to attach, and “failed to boot” was the result. 
There was also a second cause worth including:

The second time, the ISO was attached, but Windows waits a few seconds for “Press any key to boot from CD or DVD”. When nobody pressed a key,
it moved on to the empty hard disk, found nothing, and dropped into the UEFI startup menu. I fixed it by going into Boot Manager and choosing the CD-ROM drive.
The automatic install didn’t take effect either, which is why it asked for a product key. I finished the setup manually instead.

Lesson learned: My gaming laptop is not as fast as I thought, confirm the ISO download is complete before creating the VM
